# Upstream paths the fork drops. migrations/003-overlay.sh removes each one
# before it copies the overlay, and a path here cannot also be overlaid.
#
# global_noop.phpt pins the no-op phpx reverses; the fork's fixture for the
# binding is tests/fixtures/runtime/global_binding.phpt, added by the overlay.
tests/fixtures/runtime/global_noop.phpt

# extends_noop.phpt and parent_refused.phpt pin the no-op phpx reverses: the
# fork inherits the parent's members and resolves parent::. phpx/testdata/
# inheritance settles both behaviours against php in one fixture, so no
# replacement sits in tests/fixtures.
tests/fixtures/oop/extends_noop.phpt
tests/fixtures/oop/parent_refused.phpt

# interface_constants_not_acquired.phpt and interface_constants_extends.phpt
# pin the interface constant divergence phpx reverses: the implementing class
# reads an interface's constant and an extending interface answers its parent's.
# Both fixtures describe php's answer in their own description. phpx/testdata/
# interfaces settles php's behaviour in one fixture.
tests/fixtures/oop/interface_constants_not_acquired.phpt
tests/fixtures/oop/interface_constants_extends.phpt

# new_self_refused.phpt and new_static_refused.phpt pin the won't-build rows
# for `new self` and `new static`. The fork resolves both: `self` to the class
# that wrote the body, `static` to the called class. phpx/testdata/classes/
# late_static_binding.phpt settles both against php.
tests/fixtures/oop/new_self_refused.phpt
tests/fixtures/oop/new_static_refused.phpt

# unset_native_slice_reindexes.phpt pins that explode() answers a Go slice, which
# renumbers on unset. The fork wraps explode, str_split, preg_split and file to
# return a script array (stdlib/phpx/arrays_result.go), so php's numbering holds;
# phpx/testdata/functions/explode_array_test.php settles it against php.
tests/fixtures/arrays/unset_native_slice_reindexes.phpt

# TestFOpenUnimplementedWrapper in stdlib/files/csv_test.go pinned php://memory as
# false. The fork opens php://stdout, stderr, memory and temp (stdlib/files/
# phpx_wrappers.go; sebastian/diff writes its output to php://memory), so the
# overlay of that file asks about php://filter, which stays unopened.

# json_encode_flags.phpt pins that no JSON_* constant exists and that naming one
# raises. Code written for php names JSON_THROW_ON_ERROR and the JSON_ERROR_*
# codes, so the fork defines them (stdlib/phpx/constants.go); the encoder still
# ignores the flags. The two upstream tests in stdlib/core/json_test.go that
# pinned the same decision are dropped by the overlay of that file.
tests/fixtures/stdlib/json_encode_flags.phpt

# memory_alias.phpt (and TestAliasCountedOnce in stdlib/internals/internals_test.go,
# dropped by the overlay of that file) pin that `$b = $a` shares one array and
# the memory walk counts it once. The fork copies an array where php does, at
# an assignment from storage, at a by-value parameter the body writes, and at
# a return of storage (runner/phpx_value.go), so `$b = $a; sort($b);` leaves $a
# alone. The copy is counted; php shares the storage until the first write.
tests/fixtures/runtime/memory_alias.phpt
